@*
    Icon sprite. Rendered once per page by _Layout, just inside <body>.

    Why a sprite and not an icon font or a CDN: the app ships Bootstrap and
    jQuery locally and has no build step. A sprite is ~4KB of inline markup
    with no extra request, no FOUT, and it inherits currentColor, so an icon
    inside a green link is green and an icon inside a red button is white
    without a single extra rule.

    Use:
        <svg class="sab-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-box"></use></svg>

    Icons are decorative — they always sit beside a text label, so they are
    hidden from screen readers. For an icon-only button, put aria-label on
    the <button>, never on the <svg>.

    Geometry: 24x24 box, stroke-based, no fills. Sizing and stroke come from
    .sab-icon in design-system.css.
*@
